452	/**
453	 * The per-account PHP-FPM pool config (the PHP isolation boundary). Pure: given
454	 * the validated username + jailed paths, returns the exact pool file contents.
455	 *
456	 * open_basedir is scoped to the account home (+ the shared PHP lib) and NO
457	 * LONGER includes `/tmp`: PHP's tmp/session dirs are redirected into the home,
458	 * so a world-writable `/tmp` on open_basedir was just an unnecessary shared
459	 * surface between tenants. memory_limit + request_terminate_timeout cap a
460	 * single tenant from exhausting the shared box.
