531	/** Is this a syntactically valid MySQL account/database identifier for OUR
532	 *  generated names? Deliberately strict — only the charset our provisioner ever
533	 *  produces (`<username>_<slug>` / `<username>_mgr`), so a value that reaches the
534	 *  `mysql` command line as a flag can carry no shell metacharacters. NOT for
535	 *  arbitrary user-supplied table names (those are validated by membership against
