1483	/**
1484	 * Is this hostname already claimed ANYWHERE? A shared node routes purely by nginx
1485	 * `server_name`, and a hostname can live in THREE places — a primary domain, a
1486	 * subdomain, or an addon domain. Before this, each creator only checked its own
1487	 * table, so an addon could shadow a victim's subdomain (or vice-versa) on a
1488	 * co-located node = cross-tenant vhost takeover (security audit HIGH-1/HIGH-2).
1489	 *
1490	 * This is now a FAST, FRIENDLY PRE-CHECK only — good UX (an early, clear error)
1491	 * but NOT trusted alone: a non-atomic read can't stop two concurrent requests
1492	 * from both passing it and both committing the same server_name (the co-tenant
1493	 * vhost-shadowing TOCTOU). The authoritative guard is the atomic UNIQUE(hostname)
1494	 * insert into HostingHostnameClaim done INSIDE each creator's transaction — a
1495	 * colliding claim fails there (P2002) and rolls the whole tx back.
1496	 */

